======================================================================================================================
VERDICT
======================================================================================================================
  Each disc got its own QUMOND curl template from a 3-D density inverted from its own g_bar.  The razor-thin Hankel
  inversion reproduces an exact exponential to 0.04 dex but matches only 37 of 88 real profiles to 5 percent -- the
  rest have bumpy or centrally-negative gas terms it cannot follow -- so the sample is the smooth-profile third.
  On it the fitted amplitude is A = -0.98 with bootstrap +/- 0.32 but a shuffle floor of 0.53: the model
  FAILS its own identifiability bar, and A = -1 is a value NEITHER arm predicts.  It must not be quoted as a fork
  verdict.  What it is reporting is a SIGN: modified gravity's curl requires the inner disc below the algebraic
  relation, and the data sit above it, at 9.1 sigma in the 0.7-2 R_d band with a galaxy-correlation-inflated
  error.  That sign disagreement is amplitude-free and is the robust result of f16, f17 and this file together.
  It disfavours the modified-gravity curl field.  It does NOT confirm modified inertia at three sigma, because the
  positive inner residual is unexplained by modified inertia too.  Per-galaxy templates DID shrink the bootstrap
  (0.51 -> 0.32) as promised, and exposed that the remaining structure is not the curl's shape at all.

